## Bytes

Per pause on average: bf16 history 2,243 MB; resident int2 0.200 and int3 0.262 of bf16; uniform int3's one-time extra reload over int2: 139 MB (0.062 of bf16).

Moved per turn = bytes fetched at every step, summed over the turn's steps (no reuse across steps). Unique per turn = distinct (layer, head, token) pairs fetched over the turn (what a fetch cache would move). Both are shown as MB and as a multiple of int3's one-time extra reload on the same pause. Resident = int2 history + one step's fetched set, as a fraction of bf16, next to resident int3. spec also decodes one speculative token per step (compute, not bytes).

